-- gap[104] · the filed repro, verbatim: a condition the compiler PROVES true.
--
-- `if 42 > 10 print("...")` compiled clean and printed NOTHING. Two lines in
-- the body, because the second one is the block's TAIL EXPRESSION and that is
-- the slot the defect lived in — a one-line body would have been green against
-- the bug on the `arms` shape and is not evidence on its own.
--
-- `after` is the control: it is outside the `if`, so a run that prints only
-- `after` says the branch body was lost, and a run that prints nothing at all
-- says something much larger broke.

main = (): i64
    if 42 > 10
        print("first")
        print("last")
    print("after")
    0
